{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.Helium3Witness","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Helium3Witness","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.LightNucleus","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.WitnessR5Full"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.helium3StrictComplementarityCert","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.helium3StrictComplementarityCert","kind":"def","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/Helium3Witness.lean#L122-L131","doc":"**Strict-complementarity certificate for ³He** — constructed\nusing the empty-active-set option (since `min_block_eig > 0`\n⟹ optimum is in the strict interior). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.helium3_min_block_eig_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.helium3_min_block_eig_pos","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/Helium3Witness.lean#L117-L120","doc":"The minimum block eigenvalue is strictly positive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.helium3_min_block_eig","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.helium3_min_block_eig","kind":"def","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/Helium3Witness.lean#L111-L115","doc":"The minimum block eigenvalue across the ³He Wedderburn\ndecomposition is `0.53` (the `standard` block, tied with\n`sign`).  This is the categorical content of the\n\"interior optimum\" finding. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.instR5FullWitness_helium3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.instR5FullWitness_helium3","kind":"instance","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/Helium3Witness.lean#L77-L109","doc":"**R5-full witness for ³He** — partial instance from PR #608's\n`r5-full-canonical-knot-solver.witness.json`.  All three\nWedderburn-block min-eigs are strictly positive (1.87,\n0.53, 0.53), so the active set is empty and the optimum is\nin the strict interior of the feasible region.\n\nField source (frozen at PR #608 — see the *Witness divergence* note in\nthe module header):\n- `alpha_gap := 0`            ← PR #608 winner.alpha_gap (also `0` in the regen)\n- `rho_star := 3`             ← PR #608 winner.rho_star (regen diverged to `4`)\n- `primal_obj := 1.0`         ← **PLACEHOLDER** (PR #608's primal not extracted\n  to Lean; under strong duality must equal dual_obj). **Do NOT** wire to the\n  current JSON `cost = 0.14291` — that is the regen's *degraded single-term\n  objective*, not a canonical primal/dual (Witness divergence). Refresh only\n  from the multi-term-cost re-run.\n- `dual_obj := 1.0`           ← **PLACEHOLDER** (matches primal placeholder;\n  same divergence caveat as above)\n\nMixed sourcing is acceptable here because downstream\nconsumers (notably the empty-constraint SDP setup in\n`AppliedHelium3Uniqueness`) only depend on `rho_star_pos`\nand the alpha-gap = 0 fact; the absolute primal/dual values\ndon't enter the uniqueness conclusion. ","signatureChunk":0}]}